      "brief_text": "COMEX copper futures for December delivery closed up 10.85 cents, or 1.62%, at $6.8155 per pound on Tuesday (Aug. 25), amid concerns that the U.S. may impose import tariffs on copper, prompting traders to rush shipments into the U.S. and drawing supply away from other markets, tightening stocks outside the U.S. Meanwhile, withdrawal orders from LME warehouses added to global supply worries. The U.S. is considering tariffs on copper imports, with Trump to decide after receiving a report from the Commerce Department. If imposed, the tariff would start at 15% in 2027 and rise to 30% in 2028.",
